# =============================================================================
# EOL shield — normalise all text to LF in the working tree (windows #46 class)
# =============================================================================
# Rationale (estate hygiene campaign, 2026-09-25; mirrors the phlix-windows-client
# PR #46 precedent and the tizen/ui/contracts/hub shields):
#
# If any windows-latest CI job ever lands on this repo, git's autocrlf line
# endings (or a machine-level core.autocrlf=true) can silently convert
# working-tree text files to CRLF at checkout. Two laws are exposed:
#
#  1. tests/fixtures/server-route-manifest.json is vendored BYTE-FOR-BYTE from
#     @phlix/contracts dist/server-route-manifest.json ("Clients vendor this
#     file verbatim" — its own $comment) and audited by
#     tests/scripts/verify-route-manifest.mjs.
#  2. That same verifier scans client .brs sources with
#     readFileSync(...).split('\n') and pins per-file CHECK_COUNTS — a CRLF
#     checkout corrupts the scanner's line semantics and the pinned coverage
#     census around it.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` forces LF working-tree bytes on every text file on
# every platform regardless of core.autocrlf; git detects text vs binary by
# content (NUL heuristic), so binary files never convert. Committed blobs are
# already pure LF (2026-09-25 census: 180 tracked blobs, CR only in png
# assets), so renormalisation is a guaranteed no-op and this file only FROZE
# the invariant against future checkouts.
# =============================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf
# Raster assets: byte-pinned in render/branding audits, never EOL-converted.
*.png binary
